  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "SUBTOTAL, AGGREGATE, and the D-functions reject literal numbers or arrays in their reference slots at formula entry (0x800A03EC)",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527.20088, SUBTOTAL (ref1/ref2...), AGGREGATE (reference/ref1... in reference form), and database functions (DSUM, DCOUNT, DAVERAGE, DMIN, DMAX, DPRODUCT, database argument) require actual range references in those parameter positions: supplying a literal number or array constant (such as =SUBTOTAL(9,1,2,3,4), =AGGREGATE(9,4,1,2,3,4), or =DSUM({1,2;3,4},1,{1})) is rejected by Excel at formula entry (COM 0x800A03EC) in both legacy and dynamic forms.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured by live Excel 16.0.20527 formula entry across all 18 entry-rejected rows of jnt_aggregate_arrays (rows 61-71 and 111-116) and crates/calc-fml/tests/fixtures/entry/excel-entry.tsv.",
